A||N||12||Daleford||5-sp. Izuzu to 5-sp. Getrag conversion||||1||
Z||000000||Daleford||01-09-2001||12:45 PM||||If I have a 4-cyl. 86-87 Fiero with 5-sp. Izuzu, and I am converting the transaxel to a 5-sp. Getrag, are the:<BR>Shifter and shiftercables the same?<BR>the drive axels?<BR>the transmission mounts?<BR>Speedo cabel<BR>any thing else I should know?     thanks.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheFiero64||01-09-2001||03:29 PM||||Why? the izusu is better in my book. <BR>Look at <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20001206-2-002635.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20001206-2-002635.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Will||01-09-2001||05:26 PM||||The shifter is the same.<BR>The shifter cables are not.<BR>The drive axles are the same.<BR>The transmission mounts are the same, but the mount brackets (attach trans to mounts) are NOT. The mount brackets can be had from <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A>  <BR>There is no speedo cable, but the VSS is the same AFAIK.<BR>You will need the Getrag throw out arm, the Getrag clutch slave mount bracket, and the Getrag shifter cable brackets, all of which can be had from <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A> <P>The Fier64: Why do you think the Isuzu better than the Getrag?||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||01-09-2001||08:14 PM||||I can explain that. The Isuzu is smoother and the gear ratios are better. The Getrag is notchy, first gear is a joke, and cables are difficult to find and a fortune.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Daleford||01-09-2001||08:37 PM||||OK.I'm learning.I'll consider the Izuzu. The thing is,I am building a kitcar and planned on bolting up a Cadillac 4.9 to the desired Getrag.  Does the Izuzu have the same bolt pattern as the Getrag?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Daleford||01-09-2001||09:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fiero56:<BR><B>I can explain that. The Isuzu is smoother and the gear ratios are better. The Getrag is notchy, first gear is a joke, and cables are difficult to find and a fortune.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Thanks for the help. What do you mean by first gear is a joke?  -not steep enough gear? sluggish?<BR><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000006||fiero56||01-09-2001||09:08 PM||||Bolt patters are the same on all fiero engines/trannies, doesn't matter if 4 or 6cyl. <P>If you plan to put more power down, the Getrag might not be a bad idea. You might want to check out <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com</A>.<P>First gear is just way too short IMO. When trying to turn left in an intersection I'm out of first gear before I can even cross the first lane. Its nice for off the line, but for daily use, it is a nuisance. Plus, it is hardly a close-ratio tranny, particularly the jump from first to second.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 01-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cheever2||01-09-2001||09:14 PM||||Forgive my ignorance, but what came stock on my: <BR>88 GT?<BR>88 Coupe?<BR>Both 5-spd.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000008||fiero56||01-09-2001||09:17 PM||||V-6 5-speed=Getrag<BR>I-4 5-speed=Izusu<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 01-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Cheever2||01-09-2001||09:21 PM||||Oh.  Then I like the Getrag.  But then again it's not fair to the Isuzu considering it has a 4-cyl hangin' onto it.  But the GT shifts so much smoother.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||fiero56||01-09-2001||10:04 PM||||My main complaint with my Getrag is that 2nd, 3rd, and 4th gear syncros are all shot. They all went in the last 20,000 miles(170K right now). Once the tranny fluid has had a chance to warm up thoroughly, it is better though. I've only driven one Getrag and that is mine though. Plus, when the Getrag does go bad, even a decent rebuild of just seals and syncros runs over a grand. Take into account that I have probably ground the crap out of my Getrag brass due to the bad syncros, and it isn't even worth fixing. Plus, the select cable housing on mine is cracking very badly, so it if very stiff to shift. I might have a different view of the tranny if I ever drive a better example than mine. I have found the Muncie 4-speed to be my tranny of choice, but it is missing a nice highway cruising gear, that is why I plan to change the gearing of an Izusu.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Will||01-10-2001||04:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fiero56:<BR><B>My main complaint with my Getrag is that 2nd, 3rd, and 4th gear syncros are all shot. They all went in the last 20,000 miles(170K right now).<BR></B><BR>&lt;snip&gt;<P><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You might want do drive a Getrag that isn't totally worn out and in need of complete overhaul before you bash the transmission. You probably should have rebuilt it 40,000 miles ago.<P>I have no complaints about my transmissions. They shift fast and smooth and are easy to drive. I will agree that 1st gear is somewhat lower than it needs to be.||||reg||1
Z||000012||fiero56||01-10-2001||04:48 PM||||Didn't have the car 40,000 miles ago...<P>Still doesn't change my views on the gear ratios of it. That's why I'm planning an Isuzu on my 3.4.||||reg||1
